From ddc17603694a63003890e45f23a6b2e965bffcf6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daytona0306 <y.o.19910306@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 23:50:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Follow the ZMK endpoints rename from #3140

zmk_endpoints_selected() was renamed to zmk_endpoint_get_selected() in
zmkfirmware/zmk#3140 ("feat(endpoints): add \"no endpoint\" value",
2026-02-12). Building against ZMK main therefore fails:

  src/radial_controller/endpoints.c:12:45: error: invalid initializer

The old name is gone, so the call is implicitly declared as returning
int, which cannot initialise a struct zmk_endpoint_instance.

Upstream torabo-tsuki-lp pins ZMK to v0.3, where the old name is still
correct -- this patch is only needed when building against ZMK main.
Signature and semantics are identical, and the switch already has a
default: arm, so ZMK_TRANSPORT_NONE (added by the same PR) needs no
handling.
---
 src/radial_controller/endpoints.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/radial_controller/endpoints.c b/src/radial_controller/endpoints.c
index 96b979a..cd6e20b 100644
--- a/src/radial_controller/endpoints.c
+++ b/src/radial_controller/endpoints.c
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@
 #include <zmk/hires_dial/radial_controller.h>
 
 int zmk_hires_dial_radial_controller_endpoints_send(void) {
-    struct zmk_endpoint_instance endpoint = zmk_endpoints_selected();
+    struct zmk_endpoint_instance endpoint = zmk_endpoint_get_selected();
 
     switch (endpoint.transport) {
 #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ZMK_USB)
